{"id":"119-sjres-7","label":"S.J.Res. 7","congress":119,"title":"A joint resolution providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Federal Communications Commission relating to \"Addressing the Homework Gap Through the E-Rate Program\".","latestVote":"2025-05-08","rollIds":["Senate:1:235","Senate:1:238"],"hasMetadata":true,"chambers":["Senate"],"congressUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-joint-resolution/7","metadataUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/sjres/BILLSTATUS-119sjres7.xml","metadata":{"title":"A joint resolution providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Federal Communications Commission relating to \"Addressing the Homework Gap Through the E-Rate Program\".","introduced":"2025-01-27","latestAction":"Held at the desk.","latestActionDate":"2025-05-09","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","subjects":["Administrative law and regulatory procedures","Broadcasting, cable, digital technologies","Congressional oversight","Educational technology and distance education","Federal Communications Commission (FCC)","School administration"],"sponsors":["Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]"],"cosponsors":["Sen. Thune, John [R-SD]","Sen. Wicker, Roger F. [R-MS]","Sen. Fischer, Deb [R-NE]","Sen. Moran, Jerry [R-KS]","Sen. Blackburn, Marsha [R-TN]","Sen. Young, Todd [R-IN]","Sen. Budd, Ted [R-NC]","Sen. Schmitt, Eric [R-MO]","Sen. Curtis, John R. [R-UT]","Sen. Sheehy, Tim [R-MT]","Sen. Capito, Shelley Moore [R-WV]","Sen. Lummis, Cynthia M. [R-WY]","Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]","Sen. Justice, James C. [R-WV]","Sen. Banks, Jim [R-IN]","Sen. Ernst, Joni [R-IA]"],"committees":["Commerce, Science, and Transportation Committee"],"laws":[],"committeeReports":[],"costEstimates":[],"relatedBills":[{"title":"Providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Federal Communications Commission relating to \"Addressing the Homework Gap Through the E-Rate Program\".","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/33"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2025-05-08","stage":"Engrossed in Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119sjres7es/xml/BILLS-119sjres7es.xml"},{"date":"2025-03-05","stage":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119sjres7pcs/xml/BILLS-119sjres7pcs.xml"},{"date":"2025-01-27","stage":"Introduced in Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119sjres7is/xml/BILLS-119sjres7is.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2025-01-27","stage":"Introduced in Senate","text":"This joint resolution nullifies the final rule issued by the Federal Communications Commission titled Addressing the Homework Gap Through the E-Rate Program and published on August 20, 2024. The rule permits schools and libraries participating in the Schools and Libraries Universal Service Support program (E-Rate) to purchase discounted Wi-Fi hotspots and associated mobile connectivity service for off-premises use by students, school staff, and library patrons. Under the rule, E-Rate participants must implement acceptable use policies that require hotspots to be used primarily for educational purposes."}],"actions":[{"date":"2025-05-09","text":"Held at the desk."},{"date":"2025-05-09","text":"Received in the House."},{"date":"2025-05-08","text":"Message on Senate action sent to the House."},{"date":"2025-05-08","text":"Passed Senate without amendment by Yea-Nay Vote. 50 - 38. Record Vote Number: 238. (text: CR S2813)"},{"date":"2025-05-08","text":"Passed/agreed to in Senate: Passed Senate without amendment by Yea-Nay Vote. 50 - 38. Record Vote Number: 238."},{"date":"2025-05-08","text":"Considered by Senate. (consideration: CR S2807, S2813)"},{"date":"2025-05-06","text":"Measure laid before Senate by motion. (consideration